 just a step behind  earth's strongest occasionally crossing  into the mightiest of the dragon ball  pantheon through displays of pure  rage few are liked by the sardonic  warrior prince  and even fewer are as dedicated to the  achievement of ultimate power  vegeta's dedication to martial arts and  the cultivation of his qi  are unparalleled combined with his regal  bloodline  these characteristics make for one of  the most dominant fighters in the  universe  while he repeatedly says goku is his  mortal enemy his actions show respect  and acknowledgement in the competitive  drive supplied by his saiyan companion  once sent to earth in the form of an  enemy in search of the dragon balls  his disdain for kakarot is pacified by  his desire to pass him in terms of power  he repeatedly falls short in this  endeavor as his anger  tends to overwhelm him and cause him to  rush into dangerous situations without  analysis  an extraordinarily high opinion of  himself results in vegeta  underestimating his opponents and  charging in ill-prepared  his immense amount of pride calls forth  endless pools of power  and at other times serves as a  debilitating weakness  i don't care how powerful you are i will  be the one who defeats you and  claims a super dragon ball  regardless he continues to be one of  universe 7's strongest heroes  the backstory of this stoic fighter is  wrought with death and loneliness  jiren hasn't moved a muscle yet yeah i  know what i expect him to  that's kind of a schtick the whole stoic  thing  as a child jiren lost his parents and  his entire village to a villainous demon  who  in a later confrontation also killed his  master  this resulted in a lifetime of  dedication to strength and honor  and until he joined the pride soldiers  jiren spent a large portion of his life  alone in his training the most  impressive aspect of this burly fighter  lies in his little need for much  transformation to call forth  vast amounts of energy as he's able to  sustain